      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T11:46:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I agree these paths would be useful to cover.\n\nThe difficulty is that the current implementation calls read() directly on a\nnon-blocking inotify fd. Reproducing EAGAIN or EINTR deterministically would\nrequire controlling the result of that read() call. Without adding a test seam\naround read(), the test would need to rely on scheduler timing/races, which\nwould be flaky and not suitable for upstream CI.\n\nI can add coverage if introducing a small test-only seam is acceptable, for\nexample by injecting a read function with ::read as the production default, or\nby factoring the transient errno classification into a helper. However, adding\nthat extra production surface only for this error path may be a larger change\nthan the fix itself.\n\nDo you think adding such a seam here is appropriate, or would you prefer to keep\nthis patch scoped to handling the transient errno values directly?",
      "parentUuid": "30d1b263_bc6ec934",
      "revId": "24411d124b7a5f93b1d736b2fa0ab3a8d8d7f741",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
