      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T07:08:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks — I think patchset 3 already solves this. isTransientReadError() is static and stateless (int in, bool out), so it\u0027s directly unit-testable without mocking read():\n\nEXPECT_TRUE(NotifyWatch\u003cT\u003e::isTransientReadError(EAGAIN));\nEXPECT_FALSE(NotifyWatch\u003cT\u003e::isTransientReadError(EIO));\n\n\nCould you make it public (or a free function) so a gtest in test/common/ can reach it? That covers the EAGAIN/EINTR classification I originally asked about, with no read() seam needed. Agreed the full re-arm/propagation path would need real fd mocking — fine to skip that and rely on review + your QEMU testing for now.",
